Z||000000||MooCow||03-14-2000||09:22 PM||||I found another Fiero it is an 86se v6 with 93,000 miles on it.  It comes with a 7,500/6 month mile warrenty on it and the dealer is asking 2,700 for it.  I went and looked at it and it started right up but didnt test drive it. The seat has a little rip in it but the front is a different color than the car.  I'm thinking maybe the car had a bra on and the dealer took it off or the gold paint has just faded in the front.  also he told me it has an exhaust leak.  Is this a big thing to fix or not??  Should I get it??   Plus I also need help trying to convince my parents into letting me get it.<BR>                        Thanks Ken||||reg||6
Z||000001||JetroGT||03-16-2000||05:11 AM||||Gold paint on Fieros seem to fade the most.  Is the exhaust leak on the manifolds or on the exhaust pipes?<BR>Also, what kind of options does the car come with? cruse, pm, pw?<P>Have the dealer or a friend start it and look for white smoke at startup. That will tell you how worn the valves are. Look for any fresh puddles under the car. <P>If it runs, handels, and looks good I'd go for it!||||reg||14
